<title>PERU: UNILEVER BUYS PERU'S PACOCHA.</title>
<headline>UNILEVER BUYS PERU'S PACOCHA.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Dutch Unilever NV-Plc bought the remaining 49.9 percent stake in Peru's Pacocha S.A. for about $41 million to become the sole owner of the industrial company, officials said Friday.</p>
<p>Unilever already owned 50.1 percent of Pacocha, which manufactures and sells household products and foodstuffs, Jorge Licetti, Pacocha's vice president, said.</p>
<p>Pacocha is currently trying to expand to penetrate the domestic ice-cream market and hopes to boost overall sales this year by about 10 percent to between $120 million and $130 million, according to company officials.</p>
<p>-- Marco Aquino, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
